The storage manager's "create" request ends in `.finaly(...)` — a typo for `.finally`. Calling it throws
a TypeError, so `isCreating` is never reset: whenever creating a storage fails (and with the read-only
storage manager it always does, on purpose) the panel stays on "Creation in progress..." for good and
the user has no way back except closing it. With the typo fixed the panel returns to the form after the
error toast, which is what the toast's message is for.

--- a/src/components/Storage/StorageManagerPanel.vue
+++ b/src/components/Storage/StorageManagerPanel.vue
@@ -539,7 +539,7 @@
 					type: 'is-danger'
 				})
 				console.error(err)
-			}).finaly(() => {
+			}).finally(() => {
 				this.isCreating = false
 			})
 		},
